#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map to quantum problem {#step-1-map-to-quantum-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Étape 1 : Mapper vers le problème quantique {#step-1-map-to-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1a: Setting up our Hamiltonian {#1a-setting-up-our-hamiltonian}"
msgstr ""
"1a : Mise en place de notre Hamiltonien {#1a-setting-up-our-hamiltonian}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We use the Ising model on a line of 10 sites:\n"
msgstr "Nous utilisons le modèle d'Ising sur une chaîne de 10 sites :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}_{\\text{Ising}} = \\sum_{i=1}^{9} J_{i,(i+1)} Z_i Z_{(i+1)} + \\sum_{i=1}^{10} h_i X_i \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}_{\\text{Ising}} = \\sum_{i=1}^{9} J_{i,(i+1)} Z_i Z_{(i+1)} + \\sum_{i=1}^{10} h_i X_i \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $J$ is the coupling strength between two sites and $h$ is the external magnetic field.\n"
"The [qiskit_addon_utils](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/) package provides some reusable functionalities for various purposes.\n"
msgstr ""
"où $J$ est la force de couplage entre deux sites et $h$ est le champ magnétique externe.\n"
"Le paquet [qiskit_addon_utils](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/) fournit des fonctionnalités réutilisables pour diverses applications.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Its [qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/stubs/qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators.html) module provides functions to generate Heisenberg-like Hamiltonians on a given connectivity graph.\n"
"This graph can be either a [rustworkx.PyGraph](https://www.rustworkx.org/apiref/rustworkx.PyGraph.html) or a [CouplingMap](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap) making it easy to use in Qiskit-centric workflows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Son module [qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/stubs/qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators.html) fournit des fonctions pour générer des Hamiltoniens de type Heisenberg sur un graphe de connectivité donné.\n"
"Ce graphe peut être soit un [rustworkx.PyGraph](https://www.rustworkx.org/apiref/rustworkx.PyGraph.html), soit un [CouplingMap](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap), ce qui le rend facile à utiliser dans des flux de travail centrés sur Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the following, we create a simple line of 10 qubits using the "
"`CouplingMap.from_line` method.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dans ce qui suit, nous créons une simple chaîne de 10 qubits en utilisant la"
" méthode `CouplingMap.from_line`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "![Code output](/img/qiskit-addons/mpf/01-getting-started/output_1.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Code output](/img/qiskit-addons/mpf/01-getting-started/output_1.png)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we generate the "
"[SparsePauliOp](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp)"
" on the provided connectivity with the desired constants.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ensuite, nous générons le "
"[SparsePauliOp](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp)"
" sur la connectivité fournie avec les constantes désirées.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The observable that we will be measuring is the total magnetization which we"
" can simply construct as shown below:\n"
msgstr ""
"L'observable que nous allons mesurer est la magnétisation totale, que nous "
"pouvons simplement construire comme indiqué ci-dessous :\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1b: Multi-Product Formulas {#1b-multi-product-formulas}"
msgstr "1b : Formules multi-produits {#1b-multi-product-formulas}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"MPFs reduce the Trotter error of Hamiltonian dynamics through a weighted "
"combination of several circuit executions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Les MPFs réduisent l'erreur de Trotter de la dynamique hamiltonienne grâce à"
" une combinaison pondérée de plusieurs exécutions de circuits.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "To make this more concrete, we define an MPF as:\n"
msgstr "Pour rendre cela plus concret, nous définissons une MPF comme :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mu(t) = \\sum_{j} x_j \\rho^{k_j}_{j}\\left(\\frac{t}{k_j}\\right) + \\text{some remaining Trotter error} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mu(t) = \\sum_{j} x_j \\rho^{k_j}_{j}\\left(\\frac{t}{k_j}\\right) + \\text{some remaining Trotter error} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $x_j$ are our weighting coefficients, $\\rho^{k_j}_j$ is the density "
"matrix corresponding to the pure state obtained by evolving the initial "
"state with the product formula, $S^{k_j}$, involving $k_j$ Trotter steps, "
"and $j$ indexes the number of product formulas that make up the MPF.\n"
msgstr ""
"où $x_j$ sont nos coefficients de pondération, $\\rho^{k_j}_j$ est la "
"matrice densité correspondant à l'état pur obtenu en faisant évoluer l'état "
"initial avec la formule produit, $S^{k_j}$, impliquant $k_j$ pas de Trotter,"
" et $j$ indexe le nombre de formules produits qui constituent la MPF.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The key here is that the remaining Trotter error is smaller than the Trotter"
" error that one would obtain by simply using the largest $k_j$ value!\n"
msgstr ""
"L'idée clé est que l'erreur de Trotter restante est plus petite que celle "
"qu'on obtiendrait en utilisant simplement la plus grande valeur $k_j$ !\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "You can view the usefulness of MPF from two perspectives:\n"
msgstr "Tu peux voir l'utilité de la MPF sous deux angles :\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a fixed budget of Trotter steps that you are able to execute, you can "
"obtain results with a Trotter error that is smaller in total.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pour un budget fixe de pas de Trotter que tu es capable d'exécuter, tu peux "
"obtenir des résultats avec une erreur de Trotter globalement plus petite.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a number of Trotter steps which results in deep circuits, you can use "
"MPF to find several shorter-depth circuits to run which result in a similar "
"Trotter error.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pour un nombre de pas de Trotter qui aboutit à des circuits profonds, tu "
"peux utiliser la MPF pour trouver plusieurs circuits moins profonds à "
"exécuter qui donnent une erreur de Trotter similaire.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "An introduction to static MPFs {#an-introduction-to-static-mpfs}"
msgstr "Introduction aux MPFs statiques {#an-introduction-to-static-mpfs}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"_Static_ MPFs are those where the $x_j$ values do **NOT** depend on the "
"evolution time, $t$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Les MPFs _statiques_ sont celles où les valeurs $x_j$ ne dépendent **PAS** "
"du temps d'évolution, $t$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Determining the static MPF coefficients for a given set of $k_j$ values amounts to solving a linear system of equations:\n"
"$Ax=b$, where $x$ are our coefficients of interest, $A$ is a matrix depending on $k_j$ and the type of PF we use ($S$), and $b$ is a vector of constraints.\n"
"For brevity, we are not going to go into more detail here and instead refer you to the documentation of [LSE](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/apidocs/qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.html#qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.LSE).\n"
msgstr ""
"Déterminer les coefficients MPF statiques pour un ensemble donné de valeurs $k_j$ revient à résoudre un système linéaire d'équations :\n"
"$Ax=b$, où $x$ sont nos coefficients d'intérêt, $A$ est une matrice dépendant de $k_j$ et du type de PF que nous utilisons ($S$), et $b$ est un vecteur de contraintes.\n"
"Par souci de concision, nous n'allons pas entrer dans les détails ici et te renvoyons plutôt à la documentation de [LSE](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/apidocs/qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.html#qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.LSE).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can find a solution for $x$ analytically as $x = A^{-1}b$, see e.g. [Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023] or [Zhuk et al., 2023].\n"
"However, this exact solution can be _\"ill-conditioned\"_ resulting in very large L1-norms of our coefficients, $x$, which can lead to bad performance of the MPF.\n"
"Instead, one can also obtain an approximate solution which minimizes the L1-norm of $x$ in order to attempt and optimize the MPF behavior.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nous pouvons trouver une solution pour $x$ analytiquement comme $x = A^{-1}b$, voir par exemple [Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023] ou [Zhuk et al., 2023].\n"
"Cependant, cette solution exacte peut être _\"mal conditionnée\"_, ce qui entraîne de très grandes normes L1 de nos coefficients $x$, pouvant mener à de mauvaises performances de la MPF.\n"
"À la place, on peut aussi obtenir une solution approchée qui minimise la norme L1 de $x$ afin de tenter d'optimiser le comportement de la MPF.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In the following, you will learn how to do all of this.\n"
msgstr "Dans ce qui suit, tu vas apprendre à faire tout cela.\n"

#. type: Link reference
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023]: https://quantum-"
"journal.org/papers/q-2023-07-25-1067/"
msgstr ""
"[Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023]: https://quantum-"
"journal.org/papers/q-2023-07-25-1067/"

#. type: Link reference
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Zhuk et al., 2023]: "
"https://journals.aps.org/prresearch/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevResearch.6.033309"
msgstr ""
"[Zhuk et al., 2023]: "
"https://journals.aps.org/prresearch/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevResearch.6.033309"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choosing $k_j$ {#choosing-k-j}"
msgstr "Choisir $k_j$ {#choosing-k-j}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The choice of $k_j$ is up to the end-user.\n"
"In principle, any values can be chosen but some $k_j$'s will lead to a larger noise amplification on real devices than other choices.\n"
"Thus, it is important that one tries to find _\"good\"_ values of $k_j$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Le choix de $k_j$ est laissé à l'utilisateur final.\n"
"En principe, n'importe quelles valeurs peuvent être choisies, mais certains $k_j$ entraîneront une amplification du bruit plus importante sur les appareils réels que d'autres choix.\n"
"Il est donc important d'essayer de trouver de _\"bonnes\"_ valeurs de $k_j$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we will simply pick some fixed values for $k_j$.\n"
"The smallest value is motivated by the target evolution time of $t=8.0$ which normally tells us to satisfy $t/k_{\\text{min}} \\lt 1$ but empirically we know that setting it equal to $1$ usually works, too.\n"
"If you want to learn more about this and how to choose your other $k_j$ values, refer to the respective guide: [How to choose the Trotter steps for an MPF](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/how_tos/choose_trotter_steps.html).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ici, nous allons simplement choisir des valeurs fixes pour $k_j$.\n"
"La valeur minimale est motivée par le temps d'évolution cible $t=8.0$ qui nous dit normalement de satisfaire $t/k_{\\text{min}} \\lt 1$, mais empiriquement nous savons que le fixer égal à $1$ fonctionne aussi généralement.\n"
"Si tu veux en savoir plus à ce sujet et comment choisir tes autres valeurs $k_j$, réfère-toi au guide correspondant : [How to choose the Trotter steps for an MPF](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/how_tos/choose_trotter_steps.html).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Setting up the LSE {#setting-up-the-lse}"
msgstr "Mise en place du LSE {#setting-up-the-lse}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now that we have chosen our $k_j$s, we must first construct the LSE, $Ax=b$ as explained above.\n"
"The matrix $A$ depends not only on $k_j$ but also our choice of product formula (PF) -- in particular its _order_.\n"
"Additionally, one may take into account whether the PF is symmetric or not (see [Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023]), by setting `symmetric=True`.\n"
"However, this is not required as shown by [Zhuk et al., 2023].\n"
msgstr ""
"Maintenant que nous avons choisi nos $k_j$, nous devons d'abord construire le LSE, $Ax=b$ comme expliqué ci-dessus.\n"
"La matrice $A$ dépend non seulement de $k_j$ mais aussi de notre choix de formule produit (PF) -- en particulier de son _ordre_.\n"
"De plus, on peut prendre en compte si la PF est symétrique ou non (voir [Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023]), en définissant `symmetric=True`.\n"
"Cependant, cela n'est pas obligatoire comme le montrent [Zhuk et al., 2023].\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we are going to use a second-order Suzuki-Trotter formula yielding "
"`order=2` and we will set `symmetric=True`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ici, nous allons utiliser une formule de Suzuki-Trotter du second ordre "
"donnant `order=2` et nous allons définir `symmetric=True`.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Solving for $x$ analytically {#solving-for-x-analytically}"
msgstr "Résoudre analytiquement pour $x$ {#solving-for-x-analytically}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "As mentioned before, we can find $x$ analytically:\n"
msgstr ""
"Comme mentionné précédemment, nous pouvons trouver $x$ analytiquement :\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Optimizing for $x$ using an exact model {#optimizing-for-x-using-an-exact-"
"model}"
msgstr ""
"Optimiser pour $x$ à l'aide d'un modèle exact {#optimizing-for-x-using-an-"
"exact-model}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alternatively to computing $x=A^{-1}b$, you can also use "
"[setup_exact_problem](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"mpf/stubs/qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.setup_exact_problem.html) to construct a "
"[cvxpy.Problem](https://www.cvxpy.org/api_reference/cvxpy.problems.html#cvxpy.Problem)"
" instance which uses the LSE as constraints and whose optimal solution will "
"yield $x$.\n"
msgstr ""
"En alternative au calcul de $x=A^{-1}b$, tu peux aussi utiliser "
"[setup_exact_problem](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"mpf/stubs/qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.setup_exact_problem.html) pour construire "
"une instance "
"[cvxpy.Problem](https://www.cvxpy.org/api_reference/cvxpy.problems.html#cvxpy.Problem)"
" qui utilise le LSE comme contraintes et dont la solution optimale donnera "
"$x$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In the next section, it will be clear why this interface exists.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dans la section suivante, il sera clair pourquoi cette interface existe.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As an indicator whether an MPF constructed with these coefficients will "
"yield good results, we can use the L1-norm (see also [Carrera Vazquez et "
"al., 2023]).\n"
msgstr ""
"Comme indicateur pour savoir si une MPF construite avec ces coefficients "
"donnera de bons résultats, nous pouvons utiliser la norme L1 (voir aussi "
"[Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023]).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Optimizing for $x$ using an approximate model {#optimizing-for-x-using-an-"
"approximate-model}"
msgstr ""
"Optimiser pour $x$ à l'aide d'un modèle approché {#optimizing-for-x-using-"
"an-approximate-model}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It may happen that the L1 norm for the chosen set of $k_j$ values is deemed too high.\n"
"If that is the case and you cannot choose a different set of $k_j$ values, you can use an approximate solution to the LSE instead of an exact one.\n"
msgstr ""
"Il peut arriver que la norme L1 pour l'ensemble de valeurs $k_j$ choisi soit jugée trop élevée.\n"
"Dans ce cas, si tu ne peux pas choisir un autre ensemble de valeurs $k_j$, tu peux utiliser une solution approchée du LSE plutôt qu'une solution exacte.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To do so, simply use "
"[setup_sum_of_squares_problem](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"mpf/stubs/qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.setup_sum_of_squares_problem.html) to "
"construct a different "
"[cvxpy.Problem](https://www.cvxpy.org/api_reference/cvxpy.problems.html#cvxpy.Problem)"
" instance which constrains the L1-norm to a chosen threshold while "
"minimizing the difference of $Ax$ and $b$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pour ce faire, utilise simplement "
"[setup_sum_of_squares_problem](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"mpf/stubs/qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.setup_sum_of_squares_problem.html) pour "
"construire une instance "
"[cvxpy.Problem](https://www.cvxpy.org/api_reference/cvxpy.problems.html#cvxpy.Problem)"
" différente qui contraint la norme L1 à un seuil choisi tout en minimisant "
"la différence entre $Ax$ et $b$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note, that you have complete freedom over how to solve this optimization problem, meaning that you can change the optimization solver, its convergence thresholds, and so on.\n"
"Check out the respective guide on [How to use the approximate model](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/how_tos/using_approximate_model.html).\n"
msgstr ""
"Note que tu as une liberté totale sur la façon de résoudre ce problème d'optimisation, ce qui signifie que tu peux changer le solveur d'optimisation, ses seuils de convergence, et ainsi de suite.\n"
"Consulte le guide correspondant sur [How to use the approximate model](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/how_tos/using_approximate_model.html).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1c: Setting up the Trotter circuits {#1c-setting-up-the-trotter-circuits}"
msgstr ""
"1c : Mise en place des circuits de Trotter {#1c-setting-up-the-trotter-"
"circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point, we have found our expansion coefficients, $x$, and all that is left to do is to generate the Trotterized quantum circuits.\n"
